title: 'Collator protocol revamp: parallel fetching'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/11023
  
    Implement parallel collation fetching with reputation-based escalation

     Changes

      - `parallel_fetch`: Tracks escalation deadlines for each
        `(relay_parent, para_id)` group and determines when to escalate to next candidate.

      - `CanSecond::NoKeepSlot` variant: New state indicating a parallel fetch
        succeeded for the same slot. Original fetch failures return `NoKeepSlot` instead
        of `No`, preventing claim queue slot double-release.

      - Escalation logic: Launches parallel fetches from next-best collators after
        ESCALATION_TIMEOUT. Zero-reputation peers get additional delay. Respects existing
        fetch deadlines to avoid unnecessary extensions.
crates:
- name: polkadot-collator-protocol
  bump: patch
